 /docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSe_cyQG7aKsG3uFaiS_fhqIS4Pa3NA3fd58ZEaP4
 NWJwCRtvw/viewform?usp=header\n\nThe Creative Writing Program is pleased t
 o announce a reading with Stegner Fellows in Poetry and Fiction: J.L. Chen
  and Heidi Kaloustian. \n\nThis event is open to Stanford affiliates and t
 he general public. Registration is encouraged but not required. Register h
 ere\n\n____\n\nJ.L. Chen was born in Shanghai\, lived in New York for near
 ly a decade before making her home in Vancouver\, Canada\, where she write
 s most mornings and dances into the night. Working in both English and Chi
 nese\, she has published poetry and personal essays in ARC Poetry\, Litera
 ry Review of Canada\, Tupelo Quarterly\, Northwest Review\, PRISM Internat
 ional\, Queen's Quarterly\, subTerrain\, and more. A finalist for the 2025
  Robert and Adele Schiff Award (Cincinnati Review) and longlisted for the 
 2025 CBC Poetry Prize\, Chen holds an MFA from the University of King's Co
 llege and is at work on a poetry manuscript and a memoir. (Instagram @jlch
 enwrites)\n\nHeidi Kaloustian is a writer from Michigan. She holds an MFA 
 from the Iowa Writers' Workshop\, where she was the Fiction Editor of the 
 literary journal The Iowa Review. She has been the recipient of an Avery H
 opwood Award in Fiction\, a Kresge Fellowship in the Literary Arts\, and a
  Robert J. Schulze Memorial Fellowship for a first novel. She is currently
  at work on a novel and a collection of stories.
